 ### Approach
 
-Introduce a `BOTH_DOWN` sentinel that makes the single-tool-down vs both-down distinction explicit at the detector level. This lets all four callers and `external-reviewers.md` use a single conditional instead of re-deriving the logic from `CODEX_STATE`/`CURSOR_STATE` themselves.
+Introduce a `BOTH_DOWN` sentinel in the pure detector so callers share one conditional. The explanation-block last line is adapted by the detector (`BOTH_DOWN=true` → question text; `BOTH_DOWN=false` → auto-proceed notice). Callers check `BOTH_DOWN == "false"` (exact string) so empty/unset falls through safely to the prompt path.
 
-The explanation-block text change in `degraded-tools-gate.sh` (both skill-label branches, including the two-line non-design question) ensures that the block the caller prints already says the right thing regardless of whether the caller uses it as a notice or as a question preamble.
-
 ### Edge cases
 
-- `BOTH_DOWN` is always `false` when `DEGRADED=false` (trivially, nothing to branch on). Callers only consult `BOTH_DOWN` when `DEGRADED=true`.
-- The `.degraded-tools-gate-prompted` sentinel continues to fire in both sub-branches so re-entry on the same run does not re-warn or re-ask.
-- Autonomous/non-interactive behavior is unchanged: the existing `On a non-interactive run, log and proceed` branch stays as-is; `BOTH_DOWN` is irrelevant on that path.
-- Test harness: existing cases that assert explanation-block presence remain valid; Case 3 pins non-design closing lines; Cases 13/14 pin design closing lines.
+- Empty/unset `BOTH_DOWN` (partial deploy, parse failure) → callers prompt. Safe default.
+- `BOTH_DOWN=false` path writes the `.degraded-tools-gate-prompted` sentinel so resume-path re-entry skips the gate block entirely (same as the ask-path).
+- `DEGRADED=false` → `BOTH_DOWN=false` trivially; callers only consult `BOTH_DOWN` when `DEGRADED=true`.
+- Non-interactive / autonomous runs: unchanged. `BOTH_DOWN` is irrelevant on that path.
+- Per-skill Continue labels preserved: each SKILL.md caller keeps its own label in the `BOTH_DOWN=true` branch.
 
 ### Failure modes
 
-- **Updated skills:** if `BOTH_DOWN` is not parsed or not exactly `true`/`false` while `DEGRADED=true`, treat `BOTH_DOWN=true` and prompt (fail-safe — avoids auto-proceed when both externals are down).
-- **Partial deploy (old skill text only):** if the gate emits `BOTH_DOWN` but a skill has not yet been updated to parse it, the skill keeps legacy ask-always behavior — safe rollout order is gate + docs first, then SKILL.md / external-reviewers.md.
+- Partial deploy (detector updated, callers not): callers ignore `BOTH_DOWN` and ask as before. Safe.
+- Misparse (`BOTH_DOWN` empty): callers prompt. Safe via exact-string check.
 
 ### Testing strategy
 
-- `test-degraded-tools-gate.sh`: add `BOTH_DOWN` assertions to existing Cases 2–4; extend Case 3 for non-design explanation closing lines; add Cases 13–14 for design closing lines. Run: `bash scripts/test-degraded-tools-gate.sh`.
-- No new integration test needed: `make lint` already wires `test-degraded-tools-gate` into the pre-commit check.
